<spell-notebook "summary usage">
	<header level="1">
		Summary
		<header>A summary is a feed event's main line:  who did what, and when.</>
	</>
	<summary-tab-bar showing="usage"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#using-it">Using it</>
			<item link="#owners">Owners</>
			<item link="#accessibility">Accessibility</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Using it">
		<markdown>
			`<ui-summary>` is a feed event's main line: who did what, with an inline `<ui-author>` and `<ui-date>`.

			- No attributes: it takes the feed's bold-ish line style.
			- Put a `<ui-date>` inside it to show the date inline at its end, or before it to show it above.
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Owners">
		<markdown>
			`<ui-summary>` finds its nearest owner and sets `:state(in-<owner>)` on itself; `UIParts.css` styles it by that
			state. Its owners, and what each makes of it:

			- [Feed](/components/ui/ui-feed.html) (`:state(in-feed)`): the event's main line, the author bold and the date inline

			Anywhere else it is an unstyled block. More on how parts find their owners: [Content parts](/components/ui/ui-header.html).
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Accessibility">
		<markdown>- A neutral block with no role; the event around it is a list item of the feed's list.</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
